From 47343b4e8c364411324b0ce33646614215ac7033 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:28:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban worker-first: never reserve an enrolled card
 every pool worker's pickup gate refuses; repin it to its origin

Problem (t_01a1d560c6d3bc3c, 11-13, MacBook default board): t_01a1d5386cb55abf and t_01a1d54acc8c8e54 quoted
the hub CLI's task-list command in backticks as evidence. kanban_placement_coordination.requirements() reads a
backticked hub CLI action as a home-only coordination action (ACTION_REASON), so claim_refusal(), every pool
worker's pickup gate, refused both cards on every worker. They were enrolled worker-first and
kanban_worker_placement.reevaluate() reserved a worker about every 10 s for 42 and 22 minutes (lease_version
1519 and 642, 79+ queue comments listing worker-2/worker-3 as eligible). Nobody ever ran them; `kanban move
--pool` was refused too (repin_unavailable). Only rewording the bodies freed them.

Scope: PR #2339 (892a5a061a) already stops creation from enrolling such a card. This change covers the rest: a
card that is still enrolled (created by a gateway on older code, or whose body was edited after enrollment to
quote a home action outside an "Existing work checked" section) keeps looping on main.

Five whys: the card never ran because no worker claimed it -> every worker's pickup gate refused its text ->
the placement tick reserved without asking that gate -> the tick judges the card by pool membership and labels
only, while text the gate reads as an action is invisible to the Board (it never reads card text) -> nothing on
the origin side compared the two, so the reserve loop had no exit.

Fix (one shared verdict, kanban_placement_coordination.pool_refusal / pickup_refusals; new module
kanban_worker_pickup_gate):
- Placement tick (reevaluate -> _repin_target -> origin_target): an enrolled card whose text the gate reads as a
  home-only action, or whose `requires` is malformed, is never reserved. It records queue reason
  `capability_mismatch` once (one comment quoting the matched text) and an unstarted ready card is repinned to
  its origin (`runs_on machine:<origin>`, the existing creator repin route, kanban_worker_repin.eligibility). A
  Board refusal of that repin is not re-asked at the same revision; a started card is left alone without
  reserves.
- Queue reason: a Board reply's candidate whose pickup gate refuses the card (label mismatch included) is
  annotated `pickup_gate_refused` (+ missing labels) and is never shown as eligible. A queue-reason comment
  carries the capability_mismatch text only when the observation is a new transition (main's `commented`).
- Boundary: label mismatches stay with the Board's own structural `origin` return (attested registry it owns);
  this change acts only on the machine-state-independent verdicts. Unknown members, an unreadable registry,
  held/stale members and an empty pool are never refusals.
- requirements() now also reports the matched span (internal _requirements); its return shape is unchanged.
- reevaluate keeps CC 20: the not_claimable backoff moved into _backed_off, the target choice into
  _repin_target.

Proof (base b3745e62d5, which carries #2339):
- RED on main with only the new test file: 11 failed, 1 passed (the gate-accepts regression). The enrolled-card
  test reports "reserved 4 times in 4 ticks; no worker can claim it"; the started-card and Board-refused tests
  reserve too.
- GREEN: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_worker_first_pickup_gate.py 12 passed; all 108 test files importing the
  touched modules (and kanban_placement / kanban_worker_repin): 2850 passed, 0 failed. scripts/check: 19 ok.
- The kept hunks are the ones the earlier head db6d59dfcf ran 14 mutants and a 5822-row hub replay against
  (12 killed, 1 redundant guard removed, 1 equivalent; 0 disagreements with claim_refusal). This trim removes
  only the creation path (now #2339's) and resolves one conflict with main's `commented` queue-reason gate.
- Reachability: test_an_edited_enrolled_body_still_hits_the_gate pins that the incident text, outside an
  "Existing work checked" section, still makes claim_refusal refuse on main, so such an enrolled card exists.
